      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "TEX 'N' CEE (3) is the son of G1 winner Kay Cee on debut for the Parnham stable. His only trial coming into this was superb and he looks to have found a winnable race on debut. Has shown enough talent to suggest he can start his career with a bang. PEAK TYCOON (5) has trialled well either side of the debut, winning her latest trial coming into this. CJP hops on board for her return and if she runs up to recent efforts, she'll be hard to hold out. SPLINTABELLE (8) has shown good ability at the trials coming into this, being a speedy type over two 400m trials. She hasn't been sighted this time in work, though if she's fit enough on resumption, she'll take catching. SECOND DRAFT (2) is ticking along nicely at the trials and can make an impression. SWING DANCER (9) won't be far away in a suitable race on debut.",
